    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0177" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/3–949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-09">March 9,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received March 9—10:56 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>548. Vernacular press March 9 reports Legislative Yuan yesterday passed
                    resolution requesting Premier, heads of important Ministries <pb facs="0178"
                        n="168" xml:id="pg168"/> and Commissions and Ministers without Portfolio to
                    return Nanking and manage political affairs from here during period of peace
                    talks. Sent Department 548; repeated Embassy Canton unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
